   "narration": [
    "A spot of light moves across the receptive field in the ganglion cell's preferred direction. The photoreceptors and bipolar cells are activated one after another, and the bipolar cells excite the ganglion cell. Motion in this direction drives the starburst amacrine cell only weakly, so there is little inhibition, and the ganglion cell fires strongly."
   ],
   "narrationAudio": [
    "data:audio/mpeg;base64,"
